  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Three things that must not be conflated",
      "items": [
        "BLOCK prevents a future effect; UNKNOWN may describe an already attempted effect. Preserve reachable Git and necessary Attestations through actor or host loss. Re-observe uncertain outcomes, recompile and reauthorize before continuation; never replay blindly.",
        "Attestation is the sole durable semantic result, scoped by predicate, bindings, validity and verifier, never permission. Commitment, Facts and Plan are transient. Change relations and experiments are derived: no persistent workflow graph, compatibility residue, feedback ledger or memory-backed truth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Fresh admission, not inherited permission",
      "items": [
        "Required inputs: Authorized subject; Applicable authority; Compiled Commitment; Fresh observations; TransitionPlan.",
        "Applicable claims: all applicable scoped prior Attestations selected by the current plan and policy.",
        "The graph ends at an admitted actor, not an effect. Fresh lane prewrite and the resource-local effect protocol remain mandatory."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Preserve value before controlled exit",
      "items": [
        "A new Agent continues from exact results with fresh authority. Stop writers, account for unique work, preserve useful findings, retire exact owned resources and remove discharged runtime projections.",
        "Before controlled retirement, reconcile all unique work and useful positive, negative or inconclusive results into current owners or exact recoverable evidence. Declining integration never authorizes destruction; discharged retention obligations end."
      ]
    }
  ]
